# Two feasibility-study drafts in the course's study format (one "item" per line:
# item <kind> | <what> | source: <document or code, or UNVERIFIED>).
# Kinds: firmware, register, doc, gap, risk, stop, verify.

=== study: G4 - a DMA copy with the SDMA engine of an older AMD GPU (first draft)
goal: copy 1 MiB between two buffers with the SDMA engine from a Linux kernel module, then judge whether the same is possible from the course kernel
item register | SDMA ring buffer base, size, read and write pointer registers | source: amdgpu SDMA code for the chosen generation (file not yet identified)
item register | SDMA doorbell or write-pointer update register | source: UNVERIFIED
item doc | packet format of the SDMA copy packet | source: AMD's public register and packet documentation for the generation, if it covers SDMA
item gap | power-up of the SDMA block from a cold GPU (clocks, power gating) | source: UNVERIFIED
item risk | a hung engine needs a GPU reset the course kernel cannot do | source: amdgpu reset code (not read yet)
item verify | compare the destination buffer with the source byte by byte | source: this study

=== study: G6 - one triangle on the Broadcom VideoCore IV 3D core (Raspberry Pi 3)
goal: from the course kernel, clear a render target and draw one triangle with a fixed shader, then read back the image
item firmware | none for the 3D core itself; the board's closed VideoCore firmware must already have booted the system | source: curriculum 16.1 row "Broadcom VideoCore IV" (a map, to verify in D1)
item register | V3D control registers for binning and rendering control-list submission and interrupts | source: VideoCore IV 3D Architecture Reference Guide (D1), sections not yet identified
item register | power and clock enable of the V3D block | source: Linux vc4 driver power-domain code (UNVERIFIED)
item doc | control-list packet formats (binning and rendering), tile binner, QPU shader encoding | source: VideoCore IV 3D Architecture Reference Guide (D1)
item doc | memory allocation and job submission in Linux | source: Linux vc4 driver; Mesa vc4 driver
item gap | which mailbox call, if any, the course kernel needs to power the 3D block | source: UNVERIFIED
item risk | a malformed control list hangs the binner; recovery must be tested | source: Linux vc4 driver reset path (UNVERIFIED)
item stop | stop after the study if the power-up sequence cannot be documented from D1 or the vc4 driver | source: this study
item verify | compare the read-back image with ref_triangle.cpp's reference, pixel by pixel, after confirming the fill rule in D1 | source: this study
